CH = dict(num=14, title="Economic Activities Around Us", tag="Economics", theme="Primary, secondary and tertiary sectors; AMUL",
 intro="Economic activities have multiplied from farming, pottery and weaving to computers, banking and software. To understand how they work and link with each other, they are classified into three sectors — primary, secondary and tertiary — which depend on one another, as the AMUL dairy cooperative and the making of a textbook show.",
 big_questions=["How are economic activities classified?", "What differentiates these activities to be grouped into sectors?", "How are the three sectors interconnected?"],
 blocks=[
 ("h2", "14.1 Classifying Economic Activities"),
 ("ul", ["Economic activities create **monetary value** (value measurable in money). Earlier most people did agriculture, livestock rearing, making tools, pottery and weaving; today there are countless activities — manufacturing computers, mobiles and drones, banking, teaching, driving vehicles, tailoring, software, repairing appliances.",
  "Activities with similar characteristics are grouped into **economic sectors** — broad groups of activities that help a nation's economic prosperity. The three: **primary, secondary and tertiary**.",
  "Kauṭilya's Arthaśhāstra: 'The root of prosperity is economic activity.'"]),
 ("table", ["Sector", "Nature", "Examples"], [
  ["**Primary**", "People depend **directly on nature** to produce goods; extraction of **raw materials**", "Agriculture, mining, fishing, livestock rearing, forestry, poultry, greenhouse farming, fish farming"],
  ["**Secondary**", "**Processing** primary-sector outputs into other products; construction and utilities; manufacturing", "Flour mills, oil from groundnut, tea processing, furniture and paper from wood, clothes from cotton, steel and automobiles, textile and pharmaceutical factories, construction, water supply, electricity, solar power"],
  ["**Tertiary** (service sector)", "**Services** that support primary and secondary activities and people", "Healthcare, trade and logistics, communication, banking, transportation, teaching, law, hotels, restaurants, software, repair, airports, warehouses, retail shops"]]),
 ("h2", "14.2 The Three Sectors in Detail"),
 ("h3", "A. Primary sector"),
 ("ul", ["Extraction of raw materials directly from nature: grains and vegetables from farms, wood from forests, coal from mines, fish from fisheries, eggs from poultry farms.",
  "The most common: agriculture, mining, fishing, raising livestock, forestry."]),
 ("h3", "B. Secondary sector"),
 ("ul", ["Depends on primary outputs and **transforms** them, in factories and production units, into products for sale or use.",
  "Includes **construction** of buildings and roads and **utilities** — water, electricity, gas.",
  "Examples: grain → flour; groundnut → oil; tea leaves → tea; wood → furniture and paper; cotton → clothes; iron ore → steel → cars and trucks."]),
 ("note", "NOTE", "**Automobile production in India, 2022** (SIAM): passenger vehicles about 45 lakh; commercial vehicles 10.3 lakh; three-wheelers 8.6 lakh; two-wheelers about 2 crore."),
 ("h3", "C. Tertiary sector"),
 ("ul", ["Provides **services** that support those in primary and secondary activities — sometimes unseen but vital. A truck driver carries grain and vegetables from farm to factory or market.",
  "Vendors sell produce to households; doctors, nurses, teachers, lawyers, pilots serve people; technicians and mechanics repair phones, TVs, cars, tractors; electricians keep power on; communication, software, hotels, banks, schools, hospitals, airports, shops, warehouses.",
  "Also called the **service sector**. **Warehouse** = large building for storing products before sale."]),
 ("h2", "14.3 Interdependence of Sectors: AMUL"),
 ("steps", [
  ("Problem before 1946", "In the 1940s farmers of Anand (Gujarat) sold milk to nearby villages, walking or cycling in the heat. Milk spoils fast, so they sold in a hurry or to **middlemen** who bought in bulk at low prices; farmers felt cheated and harassed."),
  ("Advice of Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel", "The farmers approached him; he advised them to form a **cooperative** to become independent of middlemen and manage collection, processing and distribution themselves."),
  ("AMUL set up, 1946", "**Anand Milk Union Limited (AMUL)** was set up under **Tribhuvandas Patel** (lawyer and freedom fighter) and **Dr Verghese Kurien** (engineer). Farmers, including women, jointly decided on production, pasteurisation and sale; income rose and middlemen were no longer needed."),
  ("Growth", "A factory was set up in Anand to make butter and milk powder; today many processing plants across India produce a wide range of products, sold in retail shops and exported."),
  ("Sector mapping", "Milking cows and selling milk = **primary**. Processing milk into milk powder, ghee, cheese, butter in factories = **secondary**. Transport by trucks, rail, air and ship, trading and retail stores = **tertiary**.")]),
 ("note", "DEFINITION", "**Cooperative** — a group of people who voluntarily come together to meet economic and social needs in a formal way; they own it and decide collectively. **Middlemen** — buy from producers and sell to consumers for a fee. **Pasteurisation** — heating milk to a specific temperature to kill harmful bacteria. **Retail** — sale of goods in small quantities to the final consumer. **Export** — goods sold to another country."),
 ("p", "Other milk cooperatives: **Nandini** (Karnataka), **Mother Dairy** (Delhi-NCR), **Aavin** (Tamil Nadu), **Vijaya** (Andhra Pradesh), **Kevi** (Nagaland), **Sudha** (Bihar), **Verka** (Punjab)."),
 ("h3", "From tree to textbook"),
 ("ul", ["**Primary:** trees are cut to obtain wood pulp. **Secondary:** pulp is converted into paper, which is printed and bound into books. **Tertiary:** transport, distribution, sale, and services such as designing and publishing.",
  "None of this would be possible unless all three sectors work together.",
  "**Recycling** one tonne of paper saves **17 trees** and **2.5 cubic metres** of landfill space, and uses **70% less energy and water** than making paper from pulp. Use paper judiciously."]),
 ("h2", "14.4 Comparison and Quick Reference"),
 ("table", ["Feature", "Primary", "Secondary", "Tertiary"], [
  ["Meaning", "Extracting raw materials from nature", "Processing raw materials into finished goods", "Providing services"],
  ["Dependence", "Depends on natural resources", "Depends on primary sector", "Supports primary and secondary sectors"],
  ["Examples", "Farming, fishing, mining", "Mills, factories, construction", "Banking, transport, teaching"],
  ["AMUL", "Milking cows", "Making butter, powder", "Transport and retail"]]),
 ("qa", [
  ("Why are economic activities classified into sectors?", "To understand how they function and how they are linked."),
  ("Define the primary sector with two examples.", "Activities that extract raw materials directly from nature, e.g. farming and mining."),
  ("What is the secondary sector?", "Activities that process primary outputs into products, plus construction and utilities, e.g. flour mills, factories."),
  ("Why is the tertiary sector called the service sector?", "Because it provides services that support primary and secondary activities."),
  ("How does the secondary sector depend on the tertiary sector?", "It needs transport, banking, electricity services, marketing and repair to run and sell goods."),
  ("Why did farmers of Anand form a cooperative?", "To avoid middlemen who paid low prices and to control milk collection, processing and sale."),
  ("Who advised the farmers and who led AMUL?", "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel advised; Tribhuvandas Patel and Dr Verghese Kurien led."),
  ("What is a cooperative?", "A voluntary group that owns and manages an economic enterprise collectively."),
  ("Classify milking, making butter and trucking milk.", "Primary, secondary and tertiary respectively."),
  ("How are the three sectors involved in making a textbook?", "Wood pulp from trees (primary), paper and printing (secondary), transport and sale (tertiary)."),
  ("Why is recycling paper beneficial?", "Saves trees, landfill space, energy and water."),
  ("Name two other milk cooperatives.", "Nandini (Karnataka), Aavin (Tamil Nadu), Mother Dairy, Sudha, Verka and others.")]),
 ],
 takeaways=["Economic activities are grouped into **primary, secondary and tertiary** sectors.",
  "**Primary** = raw materials from nature; **secondary** = processing and manufacturing; **tertiary** = services.",
  "The three sectors are **interdependent** — AMUL and the textbook show how all work together.",
  "**Cooperatives** like AMUL give producers control and remove middlemen.",
  "Recycling and judicious use of resources help sustain economic life."])
